Package: shapCopula
Type: Package
Title: Semiparametric Inference for Conditional Shapley Feature Importance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Agostino",
        family = "Gnasso",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
        email = "agostino.gnasso@unina.it",
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8046-3923"))
Maintainer: Agostino Gnasso <agostino.gnasso@unina.it>
Description: Implements the one-step cross-fitted estimator for Conditional
    SAGE (Shapley Additive Global importancE) values introduced in Gnasso
    (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2609.10313>. The conditional value function
    E[f(X) | X_S = x_S] is estimated via a Gaussian copula with empirical
    marginals (default) or a nonparametric vine copula ('rvinecopulib').
    The estimator uses K-fold cross-fitting and a U-statistic debiasing step
    to yield asymptotically valid Wald confidence intervals and two-sided
    hypothesis tests for global feature importance. A marginal
    (interventional) SAGE baseline is included for comparison with standard
    SHAP-based attributions.
